<title>KENYA: Kenya tea prices ease at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Kenya tea prices ease at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>MOMBASA, Kenya 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenyan tea prices were easier on average at the weekly auction in Mombasa, auction officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Brighter and Medium BP1s eased by five U.S. cents while Brighter and Medium PF1s shed 6-13 cents. Brighter PDUSTs dropped by 3-14 cents while the lower mediums were barely steady. Brighter Fannings and Dusts were irregular.</p>
<p>Pakistan blenders were strong while Egypt, Sudan and Somalia were very active.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261</p>
</text>
